_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"referenced","commit_id":"b1f1b45b66cc78bc70667b5b7b97242a33e33eaf","commit_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/commits/b1f1b45b66cc78bc70667b5b7b97242a33e33eaf","created_at":"2019-06-14T14:42:01Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues/comments/502136392","html_url":"https://github.com/rclone/rclone/issues/3263#issuecomment-502136392","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues/3263","id":502136392,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwMjEzNjM5Mg==","user":{"login":"ncw","id":536803,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNjgwMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/536803?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw","html_url":"https://github.com/ncw","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-06-14T14:43:25Z","updated_at":"2019-06-14T14:43:25Z","body":"What is happening here I think is\r\n- the upload fails with a 423 error - this is when the webdav backend deletes the file\r\n```\r\n2019/06/14 12:06:50 DEBUG : rclone_appending.txt: Sizes differ (src 110 vs dst 103)\r\n2019/06/14 12:06:53 ERROR : rclone_appending.txt: Failed to copy: \"rclone_appending.txt\" is locked: OCA\\DAV\\Connector\\Sabre\\Exception\\FileLocked: 423 Locked\r\n```\r\n- the next append rclone notices that the nextcloud file is a different length\r\n```\r\n2019/06/14 12:06:53 DEBUG : rclone_appending.txt: Sizes differ (src 103 vs dst 110)\r\n```\r\n- however it can't find the file when trying to read it from next cloud back to the cache\r\n```\r\n2019/06/14 12:06:53 ERROR : rclone_appending.txt: Failed to copy: failed to open source object: File with name rclone_appending.txt could not be located: Sabre\\DAV\\Exception\\NotFound: 404 Not Found\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe DELETE is issued from the webdav backend when a PUT request fails.\r\n\r\n```\r\n\tif err != nil {\r\n\t\t// Give the WebDAV server a chance to get its internal state in order after the\r\n\t\t// error.  The error may have been local in which case we closed the connection.\r\n\t\t// The server may still be dealing with it for a moment. A sleep isn't ideal but I\r\n\t\t// haven't been able to think of a better method to find out if the server has\r\n\t\t// finished - ncw\r\n\t\ttime.Sleep(1 * time.Second)\r\n\t\t// Remove failed upload\r\n\t\t_ = o.Remove()\r\n\t\treturn err\r\n\t}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis was put in as part of this change eb84b58d3c728be0834bb3bb39282346a41e6b1c\r\n\r\nSo to get some internal testing working properly\r\n\r\nI've fixed that here - can you give it a go?\r\n\r\nhttps://beta.rclone.org/branch/v1.47.0-131-gb1f1b45b-fix-3263-webdav-delete-beta/ (uploaded in 15-30 mins)\r\n\r\nI think the decision for backends to delete half uploaded files is probably a bad one and one I need to correct.  I think this affects the ftp and sftp backends too.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues/comments/502136392/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ncw","id":536803,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNjgwMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/536803?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw","html_url":"https://github.com/ncw","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncw/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues/comments/502161529","html_url":"https://github.com/rclone/rclone/issues/3263#issuecomment-502161529","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues/3263","id":502161529,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwMjE2MTUyOQ==","user":{"login":"wlohman-surfsara","id":40830735,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwODMwNzM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40830735?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlohman-surfsara","html_url":"https://github.com/wlohman-surfsara","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlohman-surfsara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlohman-surfsara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlohman-surfsara/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlohman-surfsara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlohman-surfsara/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlohman-surfsara/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlohman-surfsara/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlohman-surfsara/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlohman-surfsara/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-06-14T15:49:34Z","updated_at":"2019-06-14T15:49:34Z","body":"Excellent! Thanks!\r\nI tried it, and now, I was able to run that append loop a few times without issues. But it seems the problem is not gone yet.\r\n\r\nOne of my tests started complaining about file corruption:\r\n```\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:39 DEBUG : &{rclone_appending-beta2.txt (rw)}: Release: \r\n2019/06/14 17:20:39 DEBUG : rclone_appending-beta2.txt(0xc00046d920): RWFileHandle.Release closing\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:39 DEBUG : rclone_appending-beta2.txt(0xc00046d920): close: \r\n2019/06/14 17:20:39 DEBUG : rclone_appending-beta2.txt(0xc00046d920): not modified so not transferring\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:39 DEBUG : rclone_appending-beta2.txt(0xc00046d920): >close: err=<nil>\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:39 DEBUG : &{rclone_appending-beta2.txt (rw)}: >Release: err=<nil>\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:39 DEBUG : fuse: -> [ID=0x6c0] Release\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:39 DEBUG : fuse: <- Flush [ID=0x6c2 Node=0x4 Uid=0 Gid=0 Pid=5753] 0x2 fl=0x0 lk=0xdc5111b9253357c6\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:39 DEBUG : &{rclone_appending-beta2.txt (rw)}: Flush: \r\n2019/06/14 17:20:39 DEBUG : &{rclone_appending-beta2.txt (rw)}: >Flush: err=<nil>\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:39 DEBUG : fuse: -> [ID=0x6c2] Flush\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:40 DEBUG : fuse: <- Write [ID=0x6c3 Node=0x4 Uid=0 Gid=0 Pid=5753] 0x2 7 @61 fl=0 lock=0 ffl=OpenWriteOnly+OpenAppend\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:40 DEBUG : &{rclone_appending-beta2.txt (rw)}: Write: len=7, offset=61\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:40 DEBUG : rclone_appending-beta2.txt: Couldn't find file - need to transfer\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:40 ERROR : rclone_appending-beta2.txt: corrupted on transfer: sizes differ 54 vs 61\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:40 INFO  : rclone_appending-beta2.txt: Removing failed copy\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:40 DEBUG : &{rclone_appending-beta2.txt (rw)}: >Write: written=0, err=open RW handle failed to cache file: corrupted on transfer: sizes differ 54 vs 61\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:40 DEBUG : fuse: -> [ID=0x6c3] Write error=EIO: open RW handle failed to cache file: corrupted on transfer: sizes differ 54 vs 61\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:40 DEBUG : fuse: <- Flush [ID=0x6c4 Node=0x4 Uid=0 Gid=0 Pid=5753] 0x2 fl=0x0 lk=0xdc5111b9253357c6\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:40 DEBUG : &{rclone_appending-beta2.txt (rw)}: Flush: \r\n2019/06/14 17:20:40 DEBUG : &{rclone_appending-beta2.txt (rw)}: >Flush: err=<nil>\r\n2019/06/14 17:20:40 DEBUG : fuse: -> [ID=0x6c4] Flush\r\n```\r\n\r\nFrom the client side, the file is now only partially readable:\r\n```\r\ncat /mnt/rclone/rclone_appending-beta2.txt\r\nrun 1\r\nrun 2\r\nrun 3\r\nrun 4\r\nrun 5\r\nrun 6\r\nrun 7\r\nrun 8\r\nrun 9\r\nrun 10\r\ncat: /mnt/rclone/rclone_appending-beta2.txt: Input/output error\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd on the server:\r\n```\r\n10.255.0.2 -  [14/Jun/2019:17:20:31 +0200] \"PUT /remote.php/nonshib-webdav/rclone_appending-beta2.txt HTTP/1.1\" 204 - \"-\" \"rclone/v1.47.0-131-gb1f1b45b-fix-3263-webdav-delete-beta\" microsecs:2601331 response_size:0 bytes_received:666 bytes_sent:945 XQO7P1i7UxbKFqghXtJCPgAAAIs - 17982\r\n10.255.0.3 -  [14/Jun/2019:17:20:34 +0200] \"PROPFIND /remote.php/nonshib-webdav/rclone_appending-beta2.txt HTTP/1.1\" 207 739 \"-\" \"rclone/v1.47.0-131-gb1f1b45b-fix-3263-webdav-delete-beta\" microsecs:370438 response_size:739 bytes_received:783 bytes_sent:1657 XQO7Qli7UxbKFqghXtJCPwAAAIs - 17982\r\n10.255.0.3 -  [14/Jun/2019:17:20:34 +0200] \"PUT /remote.php/nonshib-webdav/rclone_appending-beta2.txt HTTP/1.1\" 423 246 \"-\" \"rclone/v1.47.0-131-gb1f1b45b-fix-3263-webdav-delete-beta\" microsecs:2360389 response_size:246 bytes_received:673 bytes_sent:1112 XQO7Qli7UxbKFqghXtJCQAAAAIs - 17982\r\n10.255.0.2 -  [14/Jun/2019:17:20:37 +0200] \"GET /remote.php/nonshib-webdav/rclone_appending-beta2.txt HTTP/1.1\" 200 61 \"-\" \"rclone/v1.47.0-131-gb1f1b45b-fix-3263-webdav-delete-beta\" microsecs:1648823 response_size:61 bytes_received:460 bytes_sent:1203 XQO7RVi7UxbKFqghXtJCQQAAAIs - 17982\r\n10.255.0.2 -  [14/Jun/2019:17:20:37 +0200] \"GET /remote.php/nonshib-webdav/rclone_appending-beta2.txt HTTP/1.1\" 200 61 \"-\" \"rclone/v1.47.0-131-gb1f1b45b-fix-3263-webdav-delete-beta\" microsecs:1648823 response_size:61 bytes_received:460 bytes_sent:1203 XQO7RVi7UxbKFqghXtJCQQAAAIs - 17982\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nAbout that sleep, ownCloud does some processing after a file upload has been received by the server. And if ownCloud has an objectstore as backend (as opposed to a local filesystem), it needs to upload the file to the objectstore as well. From the client perspective, this is seen as part of the PUT. It's best not to expect that this will be a quick and fast process.\r\n\r\nSince from the client side it's impossible to know what storage backend is behind ownCloud, a possible solution might be to retry n times when the error returned is 423?\r\n\r\nNot sure if that is a proper solution, I'm just trying to think around the problem that there is so much processing going on behind the scenes that make the process unpredictably slow for the client.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rclone/rclone/issues/comments/502161529/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"wlohman-surfsara","id":40830735,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwODMwNzM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40830735?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://ap